answer:
**1234 × 567**

Use the distributive (break‑down) method:  

\[
567 = 500 + 60 + 7
\]

\[
\begin{aligned}
1234 \times 500 &= 1234 \times 5 \times 100 = 6170 \times 100 = \boxed{617\,000} \\[4pt]
1234 \times 60 &= 1234 \times 6 \times 10 = 7404 \times 10 = \boxed{74\,040} \\[4pt]
1234 \times 7 &= \boxed{8\,638}
\end{aligned}
\]

Now add the three partial products:

\[
\begin{aligned}
617\,000 + 74\,040 &= 691\,040 \\[4pt]
691\,040 + 8\,638 &= \boxed{699\,678}
\end{aligned}
\]

So,

\[
\boxed{1234 \times 567 = 699\,678}
\]

